The chaincode uses `time.Now()` to generate a timestamp that is stored in the ledger. In Hyperledger Fabric, **all endorsing peers must produce identical read-write sets** for a transaction to be validated. Since each peer executes the chaincode independently, `time.Now()` will return different values on each peer, causing:

